node.doctext:
Thank you for the welcome and the very clear explanation! This worked brilliantly for me (and probably saved me a lot of time in the future). 
<p> Just out of curiosity, I went back and tried to solve the original problem with the regex after your tip about the "while" element only reading one line. You were absolutely right, and I should have been writing the following:

<code>
open( FILE, "C:/Users/li/data_collection/posts/165644996453.html" ) || die "couldn't open\n";

while ( <FILE> ) {
    $data .= $_;
}

if ( $data =~ m/(?<=<p>)(.*)(?=<\/p>\s+<footer>)/g ) {
    print "$1\n";

}

</code>

(code taken from [dsb]'s answer in [id://53830]).
</p> 
Thanks again!
